# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AutoLedger .dockerignore
#
# The Dockerfile uses `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into
# the image. Before v2.1.2 there was no .dockerignore, and the image carried
# the live data/ directory (secret.key, session.key, auth.json and every cost
# record), plus .env and the whole .git history. At runtime the /data volume
# hides that copy, but anyone holding the image (`docker save`, a registry
# push, a shared host) could read the keys straight out of a layer.
#
# Rule: the image gets application code only. Runtime state lives on the /data
# volume (DATA_DIR); configuration arrives through the environment.
# `make image-check` verifies the sensitive paths are absent from a fresh build.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Runtime state and secrets: must never enter an image layer.
data/
.env
.env.*
*.key

# Version control and editor/OS noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.claude/

# Development-only: tests, tooling, caches, docs. Not needed to run the app.
tests/
docs/
requirements-dev.txt
pyproject.toml
Makefile
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.log

# Build definition and prose docs (not read by the running app).
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
*.md
